daily record highs, 2 daily record lows","records":"Harrisburg has nearly stopped setting record lows","change":"Harrisburg's days and nights both warmed. Days warmed faster.","rain":"Harrisburg has gotten wetter"},"text":{"lede":"Yesterday's high of 45\u00b0F was typical for November 13.","t_yest":"November 13 was a typical day","p_yest":"The high of <strong>45\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13. The normal high for the date is 54\u00b0F, and the record is 72\u00b0F (1902, 1964). The low of <strong>40\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Harrisburg has nearly stopped setting record lows","p_rec":"If Harrisburg's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Harrisburg has set <strong class=\"sig\">29 standing record lows</strong>, far fewer than the 71 that chance alone would give, and <strong>77 record highs</strong>, close to the 71 that chance alone would give. The 1940s hold the most record highs of any decade (54). Harrisburg's all-time high is 107\u00b0F, on July 3, 1966.","t_chg":"Harrisburg's days and nights both warmed. Days warmed faster.","p_chg":"Across 137 complete years: Harrisburg's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.09\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.03 to +0.14), about +1.2\u00b0F since 1889. Harrisburg's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.29\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.24 to +0.35), about +4.0\u00b0F since 1889.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 3 of 12 months. Highs rose in 11 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Harrisburg has gotten wetter","p_rain":"Harrisburg's yearly precipitation has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.66 inches per decade</strong> (95% range +0.35 to +0.96), about +8.9 inches since 1889. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 44.2 inches a year. The wettest year was 2011 (73.73 in); the driest, 1941 (25.52 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 6 daily record highs, 2 daily record lows"}}